[COMMENTS]
STATION,Main weir and side weir gauging a rural catchment with clay and Chalk bedrock, weed growth and u/s sluice action apparent in flow record. GENERAL: Compound Crump weir 8.5m wide in main channel with single crested Crump in mill bypass. STATION HYDROMETRY: Suffers from weed growth problems. Sluice action at mill 2.4km u/s is infrequent but evident in flow records; sluice rarely open after 1985. Multiple ratings applied to period of record. Rating shapes comparable to bankfull/QMED before they diverge. Reasonable fit to gaugings. Rating takes account of both the main weir and the mill bypass. Flows between 16.8m3/s and 24.4m3/s are non-modular and flows over 25.5m3/s are non-modular with some bypassing of the weir accounted for by modelling. FLOW RECORD: Record affected by the Waveney Groundwater Scheme between 1975 and 1979. Rating reviewed in 2022 and data reprocessed from 1980. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in August 2024 (WINFAP Files v13). FLOW REGIME: Record affected by the Waveney Groundwater Scheme between 1975 and 1979 and during some summers e.g. Jun-Sep 2022. Rating reviewed in 2022 and data reprocessed from 1980.
CATCHMENT,Clay and Chalk largely overlain with Boulder Clay. Rural, predominantly arable land.
Qmed Suitability,Gauged to within 5% of QMED. All ratings comparable to bankfull.
Pooling Suitability,Few high flow gaugings. Ratings are different beyond bankfull and neither can not be validated beyond QMED.
[END]
